      <td style="padding: 0.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #333;">Yes. Every female flower, by hand, indoors</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="padding: 0.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #333;"><strong>Gynoecious</strong></td>
      <td style="padding: 0.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #333;">Almost all female, often over 90 percent</td>
      <td style="padding: 0.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #333;">Usually yes. Field plantings add a pollinizer row for this</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="padding: 0.5rem;"><strong>Parthenocarpic</strong></td>
      <td style="padding: 0.5rem;">Nearly all female, and set fruit with no pollen at all</td>
